@{ ViewData["Title"] = "Enterprise Operations Help"; }
<link rel="stylesheet" href="~/css/enterprise-operations.css" asp-append-version="true" />
<section class="page-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">OPERATOR HELP</span><h1>Enterprise Operations Help</h1><p>Use Monitor as a bounded control plane over cached evidence. Navigation, filtering, reporting and help pages never initiate monitored SQL collection.</p></div><div class="enterprise-help-actions"><a class="button secondary" asp-controller="EnterpriseOperations" asp-action="Overview">Enterprise Operations</a><a class="button secondary" asp-controller="FleetIntelligence" asp-action="Index">Fleet Intelligence</a><a class="button secondary" asp-action="Readiness">Persistence Readiness</a></div></section>
<section class="enterprise-help-grid">
<article class="glass-panel panel-pad enterprise-help-card"><span class="eyebrow">MAINTENANCE</span><h3>Scheduled collection policy</h3><p>Active maintenance pauses scheduled collection for the target. Manual refresh remains an explicit Operator/Administrator override and is audited.</p><p>Maintenance windows are start-inclusive and end-exclusive.</p></article>
<article class="glass-panel panel-pad enterprise-help-card"><span class="eyebrow">SUPPRESSION</span><h3>Incident actionability</h3><p>Alert suppression changes actionability presentation only. It never deletes, resolves or rewrites incident evidence.</p></article>
<article class="glass-panel panel-pad enterprise-help-card"><span class="eyebrow">COLLABORATION</span><h3>Owners, notes and reasons</h3><p>Use bounded operator notes, assignees, resolution notes and reopen reasons. Credential- or connection-shaped content is rejected.</p></article>
<article class="glass-panel panel-pad enterprise-help-card"><span class="eyebrow">REPORTING</span><h3>Safe exports</h3><p>Versioned reports are cache/control-plane only, bounded by row and byte caps, and neutralize spreadsheet formula prefixes.</p></article>
</section>
<section class="enterprise-callout glass-panel"><div><strong>Need to change SQL?</strong><span>Monitor provides evidence and advisory context only. Execute administrative changes in the approved DBA tool under change control.</span></div></section>
